---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const videoId = '4AEO1smpvzs';
---

<Layout title="Mike Trounce — Fundraise Readiness for Early-Stage Founders">
  <div id="top" class="hero">
    <div class="video-frame" id="video-frame" data-video-id={videoId}>
      <img
        class="video-thumb"
        src={`https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/maxresdefault.jpg`}
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        onerror={`this.onerror=null; this.src='https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/hqdefault.jpg';`}
      />
      <button class="play-btn" id="play-btn" aria-label="Play video">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="video-caption">Click to play</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bio">
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m Mike. I work with founders who&rsquo;ve already got traction and want to raise
      angel money and make early hires. What I solve is two information problems: getting the
      word out, and keeping things up to date. Together, you and I build a
      <strong>Company Memo</strong> &mdash; a document you can read on a phone, so you don&rsquo;t
      have to talk your story through from scratch to every new person. Even better, it
      doesn&rsquo;t go stale as the story evolves &mdash; and for some of the founders I work
      with, that happens daily or weekly.
    </p>
    <div class="signature">Mike</div>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="approach">
      <span class="eyebrow">What you get</span>
      <h2>Always there. Always current.</h2>
      <p>How you access it depends on you. If you&rsquo;re comfortable with GitHub, it&rsquo;s a single Markdown file in a private repo inside <a href="https://github.com/Mike-Trounce-Organisation/company-memo-example/blob/main/fleetscope-company-memo-sample.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">my GitHub organisation</a> &mdash; you can see its history, and use it the way you already use dev tools. If you&rsquo;d rather not, it&rsquo;s a <a href="/example-memo">simple, private webpage</a> instead. Same document, same link, either way.</p>
      <p>Not everyone who reads it should see all of it. These sessions put me in an unusual position &mdash; I end up knowing most of what&rsquo;s actually going on, including things about your clients and prospects you might not want every investor to see. So the Memo can exist in more than one version: the full one for you, and versions with specific sections held back, depending on who you&rsquo;re sharing it with. Who sees what is entirely your call.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <span class="eyebrow">The process</span>
      <h2>Talk. Draft. Verify. Repeat.</h2>
      <p>This isn&rsquo;t one long interview &mdash; it&rsquo;s a loop, and the Company Memo it produces is never really finished.</p>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-a)"></div>
          <h3>We talk, in order</h3>
          <p>Around ten one-hour sessions &mdash; the story, the people, the product, the financials, the tech &mdash; each one recorded and transcribed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-b)"></div>
          <h3>Each session, an update</h3>
          <p>Every transcript updates the Company Memo directly &mdash; not a fresh write-up each time, a refinement of the one before it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-c)"></div>
          <h3>Nothing changes it unverified</h3>
          <p>I check every draft against what you actually said before it changes the Company Memo. If something&rsquo;s misunderstood, it loops back and gets corrected &mdash; it doesn&rsquo;t go out wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-d)"></div>
          <h3>It doesn&rsquo;t have a finish line</h3>
          <p>The Company Memo isn&rsquo;t a deliverable you get once and file away &mdash; it&rsquo;s closer to a Wikipedia page for your company: always live, always the current version of the truth, updated as the company changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer id="contact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get in touch</span>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:14px;">Got something worth building?</h2>
      <p class="contact-line">Send me a note &mdash; I read everything myself.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;"><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:trounceflow@gmail.com">trounceflow@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p class="foot-note">Mike &middot; Company Memos for early-stage founders</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  const frame = document.getElementById('video-frame');
  const playBtn = document.getElementById('play-btn');
  const caption = document.querySelector('.video-caption');
  if (frame && playBtn) {
    playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const id = frame.getAttribute('data-video-id');
      const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
      iframe.src = `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&iv_load_policy=3`;
      iframe.title = 'Video';
      iframe.allow = 'autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen';
      iframe.allowFullscreen = true;
      frame.innerHTML = '';
      frame.appendChild(iframe);
      caption?.remove();
    });
  }
</script>
